    "A <link rel=\"me\"> in the page's <head> does the same, and rel=\"me noopener\" counts as well: the server looks for \"me\" among the rel words of any anchor or link on the page. The address has to be your own profile address, the one in the line above; a trailing slash or a #fragment makes no difference." : "Un <link rel=\"me\"> en o <head> d'a pachina fa o mesmo, y rel=\"me noopener\" tamién conta: o servidor busca \"me\" entre as parolas rel de qualsiquier ancla u vinclo d'a pachina. L'adreza ha d'estar a d'o tuyo propio perfil, a d'a linia d'alto; una barra final u un #fragmento no fan garra diferencia.",
    "This server fetches the page itself, in the background, at most once a day per account, over http or https only, and reads the first part of it. A page it cannot reach is left unverified and asked again later, and a page that stops linking back loses its tick." : "Iste servidor obtiene a pachina por ell mesmo, en segundo plano, como muito una vegada a o día por cuenta, nomás por http u https, y leye a primera parte. Una pachina que no puede aconseguir se queda sin verificar y se torna a consultar mas tarde, y una pachina que deixa de vincular de tornada pierde a suya marca.",
    "{used} of {max} fields used. Remove one, or empty the pronouns or the support link, to save." : "{used} de {max} campos usaus. Saca-ne uno, u vueda os pronombres u o vinclo de soporte, ta alzar.",
